    "details": "<p><strong>NeuraMorphix HackForge 2026</strong></p>\n<p><br /><strong>About</strong></p>\n<p>NeuraMorphix HackForge 2026 is a 2-Day Online Hackathon organized by Team NeuraMorphix, a student-led AI initiative focused on building innovative solutions for real-world problems.</p>\n<p><strong>Hackathon</strong>: 19&ndash;20 September 2026<br /><strong>Mode</strong>: 100% Online<br /><strong>Theme</strong>: Forge the Future &mdash; AI for Every Real Problem</p>\n<p>Got an idea that can change the world?</p>\n<p>This is your stage.</p>\n<p><strong>IDEATE. BUILD. DISRUPT.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Hackathon Timeline :</strong><br />&bull; Registration Deadline: 15 September 2026 | 11:59 PM IST<br />&bull; Hackathon: 19&ndash;20 September 2026<br />&bull; Problem Statement Release: 19 September 2026 | During Opening Ceremony<br />&bull; Idea Submission Deadline: 19 September 2026 | 8:00 PM IST<br />&bull; Prototype Presentation: 20 September 2026 | 8:00 AM onwards<br />&bull; Final Round: 20 September 2026 | 2:30 PM onwards<br />&bull; Results: 20 September 2026</p>\n<p><strong>Mode: 100% Online</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Problem Statements :</strong></p>\n<p>Problem statements will be released LIVE during the Opening Ceremony on 19 September 2026.</p>\n<p>Each team must select <strong>one problem statement</strong> and build their solution around it.</p>\n<p>Solutions should demonstrate:</p>\n<p>&bull; Originality<br />️&bull; Feasibility<br />&bull; Real-World Relevance</p>\n<p><strong>️Problem statements will NOT be shared separately. Attendance at the Opening Ceremony is strongly recommended.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility :</strong></p>\n<p>Open to:</p>\n<p>&bull; Class 10, 11 &amp; 12 students<br />&bull; 1st &amp; 2nd-year undergraduate students<br />&bull; Students from any school/college/university meeting the above eligibility<br />&bull; Solo participants or teams of up to 4 members<br />Inter-school/inter-college teams allowed<br />Inter-specialization teams allowed<br />Any programming language, tech stack, or framework may be used</p>\n<p><br /><strong>Team Formation :</strong></p>\n<p>&bull; Team Size: 1&ndash;4 members<br />&bull; Inter-college teams are allowed<br />&bull; Inter-specialization teams are allowed<br />&bull; Each participant can be part of only one team</p>\n<p><br /><strong>Hackathon Format</strong></p>\n<p><br />Day 1 &mdash; 19 September</p>\n<p>9:00 AM &mdash; Inauguration &amp; Problem Statement Release<br />10:00 AM onwards &mdash; Ideation &amp; Development<br />8:00 PM &mdash; Idea Submission Deadline<br />8:00 PM onwards &mdash; PPT &amp; Prototype Presentation Round</p>\n<p>Day 2 &mdash; 20 September</p>\n<p>8:00 AM &ndash; 1:00 PM &mdash; Shortlisted Prototype Presentation<br />1:00 &ndash; 2:00 PM &mdash; Break<br />2:30 PM onwards &mdash; Final Round &mdash; HackForge 2026<br />After Final Round &mdash; Results &amp; Winners Announcement</p>\n<p>Submission Requirements</p>\n<p>Each team must submit:</p>\n<p>&bull; Project Overview<br />&bull; Solution Explanation<br />&bull; GitHub Repository Link (Optinal for School Students)<br />&bull; Supporting PPT / Documentation</p>\n<p>️ &bull; Late submissions will not be accepted.</p>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria :&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" style=\"width: 92.1539%; height: 144px;\" data-start=\"2893\" data-end=\"3141\">\n<thead data-start=\"2893\" data-end=\"2917\">\n<tr style=\"height: 18px;\" data-start=\"2893\" data-end=\"2917\">\n<th class=\"last:pe-10\" style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 18px;\" data-start=\"2893\" data-end=\"2904\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Criteria</th>\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 18px;\">Weightage</th>\n<th style=\"width: 0%; height: 18px;\">&nbsp;</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 21px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\"><strong>Real-World Impact &amp; Relevance&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</strong></th>\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\">25%</th>\n<th style=\"width: 0%; height: 21px;\">&nbsp;</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 21px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\"><strong>Technical Implementation</strong></th>\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\">30%</th>\n<th style=\"width: 0%; height: 21px;\">&nbsp;</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 21px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\"><strong>Innovation &amp; Creativity</strong></th>\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\">20%</th>\n<th style=\"width: 0%; height: 21px;\">&nbsp;</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 21px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\"><strong>Demo &amp; Presentation Quality</strong></th>\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\">15%</th>\n<th style=\"width: 0%; height: 21px;\">&nbsp;</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 21px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\"><strong>Scalability &amp; Future Potential</strong></th>\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\">10%</th>\n<th style=\"width: 0%; height: 21px;\">&nbsp;</th>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 21px;\">\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\">Total</th>\n<th style=\"width: 45.1814%; height: 21px;\">100%</th>\n<th style=\"width: 0%; height: 21px;\">&nbsp;</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Rules :&nbsp;</strong><br /><strong><strong>&bull; </strong></strong>All submitted work must be original.<br /><strong>&bull; </strong>Plagiarism or pre-built solutions submitted as the hackathon project are strictly prohibited and may result in immediate disqualification.<br /><strong>&bull; </strong>Open-source tools and libraries are allowed with proper attribution.<br /><strong>&bull; </strong>Each participant may be part of only one team.<br /><strong>&bull; </strong>Late submissions will not be accepted.<br /><strong>&bull; </strong>Participants must follow the official hackathon timeline and submission requirements.<br /><strong>&bull; </strong>Judges' and organizers' decisions are final.<br /><strong>&bull; </strong>NeuraMorphix reserves the right to update rules, timelines, or event schedules if necessary</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong> Contact:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>info@neuramorphix.com</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Powered by Unstop</strong><br /><strong>Organized by Team NeuraMorphix</strong><br /><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
